Third-party components and provenance
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

No substantial third-party source code is copied into this repository. The
plugin calls IntelliJ Platform and Gauge plugin APIs at compile and run time;
both are resolved as ordinary Gradle dependencies and neither is vendored,
bundled, forked or patched. The produced plugin artifact
(release/gauge-typed-parameters-1.0.0.zip) contains only this project's own
classes and resources.

Two items in this repository do originate elsewhere and are noted here for
completeness:

1. Gradle wrapper
     gradlew
     gradlew.bat
     gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
     gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties

   Part of Gradle, Copyright the original author or authors, licensed under the
   Apache License, Version 2.0. The scripts retain their original Apache-2.0
   headers and SPDX identifiers. Committing the wrapper is standard practice for
   Gradle projects.

       https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

2. API stubs used by the offline verification tool
     tools/local-verification/stubs/**
     tools/local-verification/kstubs/**

   These are hand-written, non-functional stub declarations (empty method
   bodies) that mirror the public API signatures of classes from:

     - IntelliJ IDEA Community  (JetBrains/intellij-community, Apache-2.0)
     - the Gauge IntelliJ plugin (JetBrains/intellij-plugins, Apache-2.0)

   They exist only so that this project's own logic can be type-checked and unit
   tested without downloading a full IntelliJ Platform distribution. They contain
   no implementation code from those projects. Both upstream projects are
   licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

       https://github.com/JetBrains/intellij-community
       https://github.com/JetBrains/intellij-plugins

